# The CENTRE's reception desk: one tile square, counter high, flat topped.
#
# Y is up, +Z is north, one world unit is one map tile. The lowest vertex sits
# on y = 0 and the model is centred on x = 0 and z = 0, so the game places it
# by its feet.
#
# Faces are wound so that (c - a) x (b - a) points out of the solid, which is
# what tools/obj2cpp.py bakes as the face normal. Get it backwards and the
# model still draws, it just goes flat ambient dark.
#
# Four faces, 8 triangles. No bottom and no north face: the camera stands
# south of the player and looks north, so the north side is never seen.
#
# 0.62 units, a little taller than the mart's counter, and white rather than
# wood. A hospital reads as one from its fittings, and a desk the same colour
# as the shop counter would just be a shop counter in a different room.

mtllib desk.mtl

v -0.52 0.00 -0.52
v  0.52 0.00 -0.52
v  0.52 0.00  0.52
v -0.52 0.00  0.52
v -0.52 0.62 -0.52
v  0.52 0.62 -0.52
v  0.52 0.62  0.52
v -0.52 0.62  0.52

usemtl desk_top
f 5 6 7 8

usemtl desk_face
f 1 2 6 5

usemtl desk_side
f 2 3 7 6
f 4 1 5 8
